{
  "title": "Ready-made JSON requests for every tool of wirdi-mcp",
  "version": "0.6.0",
  "how_to_use": [
    "Start the server with WIRDI_AI_ROOT set (see the README) and open the MCP Inspector: npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector -e WIRDI_AI_ROOT=/path/to/wirdi-Ai .venv/bin/wirdi-mcp",
    "Pick the tool named in `tool`, paste the object in `arguments`, run it, and compare with `expect`.",
    "`needs` lists what the request depends on: WIRDI_AI_ROOT (the Quran text) or a local page store built with scripts/build_page_store.py.",
    "`expect.status` is `ok` or `error`; for an error, `expect.code` is the error code. Counts quoted in `purpose` were measured on the real corpus.",
    "Numbers of ayat are in the Qaloun count (6,214 ayat). Use resolve_source_mapping to convert to the Kufian count of the Tunisian mushaf.",
    "tests/integration/test_apply_json.py runs every request in this file against the real server, so the examples cannot drift from the tools."
  ],
  "reading_context_note": "mode `waqf` stops at the end of each selected ayah only; `wasl` reads on, so the last position needs `following` (a complete reference to the next ayah of the same surah) or `null`; `stop_after_word` stops the last ayah after that many words.",
  "reference_template": {
    "corpus_id": "wirdi-ai:quranpedia:qalun",
    "corpus_version": "sha256:ece0a2b0efe44d496211c595d0a34f495413bc93f78fba8095a666e2048d1303",
    "numbering_system": "wirdi-ai:qalun-6214",
    "riwaya": "qaloun",
    "tariq": "unspecified",
    "surah": 2,
    "ayah": 1
  },
  "requests": [
